    "body": "For what it's worth, I was able to implement this as a custom segment:\r\n\r\n```toml\r\nformat = \"\"\"\r\n$username\\\r\n$hostname\\\r\n$shlvl\\\r\n$singularity\\\r\n$kubernetes\\\r\n$directory\\\r\n$vcsh\\\r\n$git_branch\\\r\n$git_commit\\\r\n$git_state\\\r\n$git_metrics\\\r\n$sudo\\\r\n$custom\\\r\n$line_break\\\r\n$jobs\\\r\n$character\"\"\"\r\n\r\n[custom.arch64]\r\ncommand = \"echo -n x64\"\r\nwhen = \"[[ $(arch) == *i386* ]]\"\r\nstyle = \"fg:white\"\r\nsymbol = \"❮ \"\r\n\r\n[custom.archas]\r\ncommand = \"echo -n AS\"\r\nwhen = \"[[ $(arch) != *i386* ]]\"\r\nstyle = \"fg:white\"\r\nsymbol = \"❮ \"\r\n```\r\n\r\nI used `x64` and `AS` (for Apple Silicon) but for now this suites my needs.",
